Bug 2077934 - Don't leave a feed busy when parsing it throws. r=edicharry

parseAsAtomIETF() indexed the result of childrenByTagNameNS() before checking
it, so an Atom-namespace document whose root was not <feed> threw a TypeError.
That bypassed onParseError() and left the feed URL busy for the rest of the
session.

Check the result before indexing it. Also catch exceptions from parseFeed()
in Feed.parse() and report them as an invalid feed, so any other parser error
also releases the feed.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332412

